From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 21:51:48 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] Games: defer the hardware context reset out of stream opening

A client that renders through libretro's GL state manager rendered to the
default framebuffer forever, silently, with no error raised anywhere.

CGameClientStreamHwFramebuffer::OpenStream() dispatched HardwareContextReset()
directly. That runs inside the add-on's own CStream::Open(), and CStream assigns
its handle only once that call returns - so throughout the reset the add-on
believes its stream is shut, and CVideoStream::GetHwFramebuffer() takes its
!IsOpen() early return and answers 0.

Early would be survivable if anything asked again. Nothing does: glsm queries
get_current_framebuffer() exactly once, in glsm_state_setup(), and caches it as
default_framebuffer for the session - and the client runs that setup from inside
context_reset. One zero there is permanent.

The request is now recorded and dispatched at the top of RunFrame(), by which
point CStream::Open() has returned and the add-on's handle is set. Costs one
frame before the client initialises.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xbmc/games/addons/GameClient.cpp | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 xbmc/games/addons/GameClient.h   | 13 +++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/games/addons/GameClient.cpp b/xbmc/games/addons/GameClient.cpp
index 8819317..b7ffcdf 100644
--- a/xbmc/games/addons/GameClient.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/games/addons/GameClient.cpp
@@ -567,6 +567,11 @@ void CGameClient::RunFrame()
 
   if (m_bIsPlaying)
   {
+    // Before the client runs, not while it is opening a stream. See
+    // HardwareContextReset() for why this cannot be dispatched where it is
+    // requested.
+    DispatchPendingHardwareContextReset();
+
     try
     {
       LogError(m_ifc.game->toAddon->RunFrame(m_ifc.game), "RunFrame()");
@@ -785,6 +790,27 @@ void CGameClient::LogException(const char* strFunctionName) const
 
 void CGameClient::HardwareContextReset()
 {
+  // Deferred to the next RunFrame() rather than dispatched here.
+  //
+  // This is reached from CGameClientStreamHwFramebuffer::OpenStream(), which
+  // runs inside the add-on's own CStream::Open() - and CStream only assigns its
+  // handle once that call *returns*. So during a context reset dispatched from
+  // here the add-on still believes its stream is shut, and every
+  // get_current_framebuffer() it makes on the client's behalf answers 0.
+  //
+  // That is fatal rather than merely early: libretro's GL state manager asks
+  // exactly once, in glsm_state_setup(), and caches the answer for the session.
+  // A client told 0 there renders to the default framebuffer forever, silently.
+  m_bPendingHwContextReset = true;
+}
+
+void CGameClient::DispatchPendingHardwareContextReset()
+{
+  if (!m_bPendingHwContextReset.exchange(false))
+    return;
+
+  CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "GAME: Dispatching deferred hardware context reset");
+
   try
   {
     LogError(m_ifc.game->toAddon->HwContextReset(m_ifc.game), "HwContextReset()");
diff --git a/xbmc/games/addons/GameClient.h b/xbmc/games/addons/GameClient.h
index e4d09e4..b1b5e81 100644
--- a/xbmc/games/addons/GameClient.h
+++ b/xbmc/games/addons/GameClient.h
@@ -234,6 +234,14 @@ public:
   // Implementation of IHwFramebufferCallback
   void HardwareContextReset() override;
 
+  /*!
+   * \brief Dispatch a hardware context reset that was requested while the
+   *        add-on was still opening its stream
+   *
+   * Called from the game loop, where the add-on's stream handle is valid.
+   */
+  void DispatchPendingHardwareContextReset();
+
   /*!
    * @brief To get the interface table used between addon and kodi
    * @todo This function becomes removed after old callback library system
@@ -327,6 +335,11 @@ private:
 
   // Properties of the current playing file
   std::atomic_bool m_bIsPlaying; // True between OpenFile() and CloseFile()
+
+  // Set when a stream asks for a hardware context reset, cleared when RunFrame()
+  // dispatches it. Written from the thread opening the stream, read from the
+  // game loop.
+  std::atomic<bool> m_bPendingHwContextReset{false};
   std::atomic_bool m_hasFrameRun{false};
   // The speed the player is running at, as a multiple of normal speed. Written
   // by the thread that changes the speed and read by the client's own, so it is
